<div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-8">
	<div class="mb-8">
		<h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2">🛡️ Error Handling</h1>
		<p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Demonstrating Blazouter's built-in error handling capabilities</p>
	</div>

	<div class="bg-white dark:bg-gray-800 rounded-lg shadow-md p-6 mb-6">
		<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4">Error Handling Features</h2>
		<div class="space-y-4 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
			<p>Blazouter provides comprehensive error handling for routing operations:</p>

			<ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 ml-4">
				<li><strong>Component Loading Errors</strong>: Handles failures during lazy loading</li>
				<li><strong>Guard Execution Errors</strong>: Catches exceptions in route guards</li>
				<li><strong>Rendering Errors</strong>: Manages component rendering failures</li>
				<li><strong>Custom Error Handlers</strong>: Implement IRouterErrorHandler for custom logic</li>
				<li><strong>Error UI</strong>: Display custom error content or use default UI</li>
				<li><strong>Retry Capability</strong>: Built-in retry functionality for failed navigations</li>
			</ul>
		</div>
	</div>

	<div class="bg-white dark:bg-gray-800 rounded-lg shadow-md p-6 mb-6">
		<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4">Trigger Example Errors</h2>
		<p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 mb-4">
			Click the buttons below to see how Blazouter handles different types of errors:
		</p>

		<div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
			<button @onclick="TriggerComponentLoadError"
					class="px-4 py-3 bg-red-600 text-white rounded-lg hover:bg-red-700 transition">
				💥 Component Load Error
			</button>

			<button @onclick="TriggerGuardError"
					class="px-4 py-3 bg-orange-600 text-white rounded-lg hover:bg-orange-700 transition">
				🚫 Guard Execution Error
			</button>
		</div>

		@if (_showErrorMessage)
		{
			<div class="mt-4 p-4 bg-blue-50 dark:bg-blue-900/20 border border-blue-200 dark:border-blue-700 rounded-lg">
				<p class="text-blue-800 dark:text-blue-200">
					<strong>Note:</strong> Error UI will be displayed by the Router component. Check the main content area.
				</p>
			</div>
		}
	</div>

	<div class="bg-white dark:bg-gray-800 rounded-lg shadow-md p-6">
		<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4">Implementation</h2>

		<h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2">1. Router Configuration</h3>
		<pre class="bg-gray-100 dark:bg-gray-900 p-4 rounded-lg overflow-x-auto mb-4"><code class="text-sm">@(@"<Router Routes=""@_routes"" DefaultLayout=""typeof(MainLayout)"">
        <ErrorContent Context=""errorInfo"">
                <div class=""error-container"">
                        <h1>⚠️ Navigation Error</h1>
                        <p>@errorInfo.Message</p>
                        <button @onclick=""errorInfo.Retry"">Try Again</button>
                </div>
        </ErrorContent>
        <NotFound>
                <h1>404 - Page Not Found</h1>
        </NotFound>
        <Loading>
                <p>Loading...</p>
        </Loading>
</Router>")</code></pre>

		<h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2">2. Custom Error Handler</h3>
		<pre class="bg-gray-100 dark:bg-gray-900 p-4 rounded-lg overflow-x-auto mb-4"><code class="text-sm">@(@"public class CustomErrorHandler : IRouterErrorHandler
{
        private readonly ILogger<CustomErrorHandler> _logger;
    
        public async Task<bool> HandleErrorAsync(
                Exception exception, 
                RouterErrorContext context)
        {
                _logger.LogError(exception, 
                        ""Routing error: {ErrorType}"", 
                        context.ErrorType);
        
                // Return true to show error UI
                return true;
        }
}

// Register in Program.cs
builder.Services.AddScoped<IRouterErrorHandler, CustomErrorHandler>();")</code></pre>

		<h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2">3. OnError Event</h3>
		<pre class="bg-gray-100 dark:bg-gray-900 p-4 rounded-lg overflow-x-auto"><code class="text-sm">@(@"<Router Routes=""@_routes"" OnError=""@HandleError"">
        <!-- content -->
</Router>

@code {
        private async Task HandleError(RouterErrorEventArgs args)
        {
                // Custom error handling
                await ToastService.ShowError(args.Exception.Message);
        
                // Set to true to suppress default error UI
                args.Handled = false;
        }
}")</code></pre>
	</div>
</div>